{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0094"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge geography/physical","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/geography__physical.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",932],["+","Its name makes a famous German pun: Harz is also the German word for resin, and amber, Bernstein in German, is nothing but fossil Harz (resin) from forests that grew some 50 to 35 million years ago – although the mountains' name actually comes from the old word hart, a wooded upland. "],["=",137]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",818],["+","Sein Name ermöglicht ein bekanntes Wortspiel: Harz ist auch das Wort für das Material, aus dem Bernstein besteht – fossiles Harz aus Wäldern, die vor etwa 50 bis 35 Millionen Jahren wuchsen –, obwohl der Gebirgsname eigentlich vom alten Wort „Hart“ für Bergwald stammt. "],["=",125]]}]},
